.TH PKG 1
.SH NAME
pkg \- namespace-native package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkg pack
.I stagedir
.I out.tar
.br
.B pkg info
.I pkg.tar
.br
.B pkg install
.I pkg.tar
.br
.B pkg list
.br
.B pkg remove
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pkg
installs software packages by composing them into the name space rather
than copying files into a shared tree.
A package is a
.IR tar (1)
archive containing a
.B pkg/manifest
file and any of the
.BR dis/ ,
.B man/
and
.B lib/
directories.
The manifest is a set of
.IR attribute " " value
lines, one per line, in the
.IR ndb (6)
style; blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored:
.EX

	name util/pkgdemo
	version 1.0
	category util
	keywords demo date example
	provides pkgdemo
	description a demo package

.EE
.PP
Installing a package does not unpack it or touch any shared directory.
The archive is mounted read-only with
.IR tarfs (4)
at
.BI /mnt/pkg/ id\fR,
where
.I id
is the first 16 hex digits of the SHA-256 of the archive, and the
package's
.B dis/
directory (and
.BR man/ ,
if present) is bound after the current contents of
.B /dis
(and
.BR /man ).
The package's commands then resolve by bare name.
Because installation is a name-space operation it needs no special
privilege, affects only the invoking name space, and is undone exactly by
unbinding and unmounting.
Each install is named by the content hash of its archive, so installing
the same bytes twice is idempotent.
.SS Commands
.TP
.B pack
Build
.I out.tar
from
.IR stagedir ,
which must contain a
.B pkg/manifest
and whichever of
.BR dis/ ,
.BR man/ ,
.B lib/
apply.
.TP
.B info
Print the content SHA-256 and the manifest of
.I pkg.tar
without installing it.
.TP
.B install
Mount and bind
.I pkg.tar
into the name space as described above.
.TP
.B list
List the installed packages \(em name, version and content id \(em read
from the packages actually mounted under
.BR /mnt/pkg .
.TP
.B remove
Unbind and unmount every installed package whose manifest
.B name
is
.IR name .
.SH EXAMPLES
Package, install, use and remove a tool:
.EX

	pkg pack stage util-pkgdemo.tar
	pkg install util-pkgdemo.tar
	pkgdemo
	pkg list
	pkg remove util/pkgdemo

.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/pkg.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR tarfs (4),
.IR tar (1),
.IR bind (1),
.IR ndb (6)
.PP
.B /doc/pkg-roadmap.md
.SH BUGS
This is milestone 1: local packages only.
There is no signature or content verification yet, no
.B /pkg
naming service, and no
.BR search ;
those are later milestones.
An installed package keeps a
.IR tarfs (4)
server process alive for as long as it is mounted.
.SH HISTORY
.B Pkg
first appeared in Inferno-rio (2026).
